    "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:46:20Z",
    "body": "There's no change for that case, it already returns `400` (if the resource width is correct). The PR only changes `naturalWidth` when `w` doesn't match the image's real width, then it becomes `sizes` instead of `resourceWidth × sizes / w`.",
